2. ICD-O codes and terms

   The morphology codes and terms in data/ come from the International
   Classification of Diseases for Oncology, third edition, second revision
   (ICD-O-3.2), final tables of 9 October 2020. The topography codes in
   data/ are those of the International Classification of Diseases for
   Oncology, third edition. ICD-O is a classification of the World Health
   Organization (WHO), which holds its copyright. ICD-O-3.2 was prepared by
   the ICD-O Committee of the International Agency for Research on Cancer
   (IARC) and WHO, and the International Association of Cancer Registries
   distributes its tables: http://www.iacr.com.fr/

   IARC's terms of use permit extracts of IARC materials to be reproduced for
   research, private study, educational or non-commercial purposes with
   limited circulation, when the IARC source is acknowledged. Substantial
   portions, wider circulation and any other use require IARC's written
   permission: https://publications.iarc.who.int/Terms-Of-Use


3. ICCC-3 groupings

   The assignment of codes to diagnostic groups and subgroups in data/
   follows the International Classification of Childhood Cancer, third
   edition (ICCC-3), and its 2017 update:

   Steliarova-Foucher E, Stiller CA, Lacour B, Kaatsch P. International
   Classification of Childhood Cancer, third edition. Cancer
   2005;103:1457-67. doi:10.1002/cncr.20910. Copyright 2005 American Cancer
   Society.

   Steliarova-Foucher E, Colombet M, Ries LAG, Rous B, Stiller CA.
   Classification of tumours. In: International Incidence of Childhood
   Cancer, Volume III. Lyon: International Agency for Research on Cancer.


